        setup: {
          players: '2 players or 4 in teams.',
          deck: '40 cards. Ranks: 1 (Ace) to 10.',
          equipment: '',
          dealing: 'Each player receives 3 cards. 4 cards are placed face-up on the table. The deal is repeated until the deck is empty.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score Gemstones by capturing table cards (by matching value or sum), by making a Shokoba (sweep) when you clear the table, and from end-of-round awards (most cards, most Coins/Diamonds, Settebello, Primiera). The first player or team to reach 11 Gemstones wins the game.',
          gameplay: "1. **Capture**: Play a card from your hand. If its value matches a single card or the SUM of multiple cards on the table, you capture them.\n2. **Example**: A player plays a 7; they can take a 7 from the table, or a 4 and a 3, or a 5 and a 2.\n3. **Shokoba!**: If you capture ALL remaining cards on the table, you shout 'SHOKOBA!' and win 1 Gemstone immediately.",
          keyRules: [
            'Capture by playing a card that matches one table card or the sum of several table cards; if both match, take the single card.',
            'When a capture is possible you must capture.',
            'Shokoba: clearing the entire table in one play scores 1 Gemstone.',
            'First to 11 Gemstones wins.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Prioritize the 7 of Diamonds. It is the most valuable card in the deck and contributes to the 'Most Diamonds' and 'Preme' points. Never play it unless you are certain it will be captured.",
          intermediate: "Preventing Shokoba: If there is only one card left on the table (e.g., a 4), and you can't capture it, DON'T play a card that sums to a high value. Play a card that leaves the table with values that are hard to sum for the next player (like two small cards instead of one high one).",
          advanced: "The 'Diamond Sweep': If you are trailing in points, focus entirely on the 'Most Diamonds' category. Even if you lose individual tricks, capturing 6 or 7 Diamonds will guarantee you 2 points at the end of the round (Diamond count + 7 of Diamonds).",
          tips: [
            "Count the 7s. There are only four. If three have been played, the last 7 becomes a powerful 'Shokoba' tool.",
            "If playing in teams, watch what your partner leaves on the table. Try to 'setup' a sum for them if you suspect they have a high-value card.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
